WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.793
Hello everyone.

00:00:09.793 --> 00:00:11.050
This is Gavin and Dan.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.130
Coming to you live from
inside the internet.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:14.963
Except it's not live.

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:15.796
It's not live.

00:00:15.796 --> 00:00:16.629
You see, prerecorded.

00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:17.870
Yeah, we're doing a voice over.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.840
We rarely do this but Dan
knows a lot about guns

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.892
and he wants to talk
about guns, don't you?

00:00:22.892 --> 00:00:23.725
Little bit.

00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:24.780
We're using a different
camera on this one.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.033
It's the V1610.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:28.950
It's the same camera we
used to shoot underwater.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:30.240
That is incredibly slow.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.070
This is at 18000 frames per second.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.050
18000?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:33.883
And you can count it.

00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:36.850
You got one, two, three,
four cases in the air.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.880
There's always like a tiny little ember

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.290
on the rim of the case.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.123
Yeah, just flying out of it.

00:00:42.123 --> 00:00:43.740
Look how the gun shakes.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.860
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.021
It looks sturdy as hell.

00:00:46.021 --> 00:00:47.700
Pretty rattley in slow mo.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.941
You can even see when
we speed it up slightly

00:00:49.941 --> 00:00:53.300
your watch is rattling
around on your wrist too.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.133
Oh, yeah.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.300
Pretty efficient machine.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.460
Every movement is for a purpose.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.480
Yeah, the firing pin
now is impacting on the

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.430
primer of the round.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.320
That fires the bullet out and
the empty case gets ejected.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.010
So it's being pulled backwards here

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.900
using the force of the gas
to pull the working part.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.451
So there's nothing
actually pulling that back.

00:01:11.451 --> 00:01:12.284
No.

00:01:12.284 --> 00:01:13.117
It's just the force of
the bullet going out

00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:13.950
that's ejected that.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:14.783
It's the gases.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.050
Yeah, that are being created.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.500
And the next round gets loaded in

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.520
when the spring on the
other side sets itself,

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.840
extracting the next
round from the magazine.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.160
I see the next round go up just there.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.360
It gets loaded into the chamber

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.140
and then the firing pin again

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:30.760
impinges on the primer of the round.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:35.210
That ignites the
propellant inside the round

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.690
and that causes the
gas to force the bullet

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:38.830
out the end of the barrel

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.010
and the case out the rear.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.101
This is my favorite part finish firing.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.410
Look how wide eyed you are there.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.243
Oh, my God.

00:01:47.243 --> 00:01:48.076
Your eyes.

00:01:48.076 --> 00:01:48.930
Whoa.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.108
Looks like you've seen a yeti.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.510
Yeah, I went back quite a ways.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.908
Yeah, you did crap yourself.

00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:02.741
Yeah.

00:02:02.741 --> 00:02:03.574
On the first shot.

00:02:03.574 --> 00:02:04.820
You literally took a step back.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:05.950
You're like.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.200
Little bits of poo poo.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:10.010
All right, so now's the part, Dan,

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:12.325
where I show you how its really done.

00:02:12.325 --> 00:02:14.400
My first time ever
firing an assault rifle.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.560
Especially automatic.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.628
I think before this I'd
only ever fired a pistol

00:02:17.628 --> 00:02:18.938
and a shotgun.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.010
There we go, first shot.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:20.900
First shot.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.570
You can see my reaction time.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:23.733
I haven't blinked yet.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.510
The round's already been
fired by this point.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.691
The round has already
probably gone through

00:02:28.691 --> 00:02:30.810
and exited the target.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:31.860
The rifle is pushing back

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.251
because you didn't have
it fully in your shoulder.

00:02:34.251 --> 00:02:35.170
Well, I didn't have it in my shoulder,

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.218
but my lean was wrong.

00:02:37.218 --> 00:02:38.051
I was leaning back.

00:02:38.051 --> 00:02:39.200
There goes the eye.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.850
I've already killed someone
and I'm just now blinking.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.280
Yeah.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.000
Still firing.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.833
Still firing obviously,

00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:47.690
I'm not going to let off the trigger.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:48.545
Yeah, sure, yeah.

00:02:48.545 --> 00:02:49.378
I'm not going to baby it.

00:02:49.378 --> 00:02:50.211
Close your eyes.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.700
Oh, nice little vent of gas there.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:55.949
Yeah.

00:02:55.949 --> 00:02:56.782
I'm going to speed it up

00:02:56.782 --> 00:02:58.100
so you can see the amount that I've--

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.800
Not in control of that at all.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.302
Well, I've never done it before.

00:03:01.302 --> 00:03:02.135
Look it.

00:03:02.135 --> 00:03:03.410
I was just told not to
let go of the trigger

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.785
so the rest of it was--

00:03:04.785 --> 00:03:06.108
Well you did a good job of that.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.520
So, now I'm thinking, right,

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.340
let's try and get this gun
back pointed towards the ground

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.650
while I'm trying to walk forwards again.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.070
Because on the other camera,

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:15.903
I'm completely out of shot.

00:03:15.903 --> 00:03:16.736
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:16.736 --> 00:03:17.960
Now the gun has gone out of focus

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.420
but you can see some pretty
shots of the cases coming out,

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.650
which is pretty cool.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.410
It's weird after you
get to the point where

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.211
you know what's going on
and you don't blink anymore.

00:03:26.211 --> 00:03:29.110
Every single shot is
like, kow, kow, kow, kow.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.090
But you just don't blink.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.212
It gets to the point where

00:03:31.212 --> 00:03:32.330
you're just used to what's going on.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:35.610
Well, there's something called a keyhole

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.150
where when you're firing on automatic

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.810
your first shot goes on target,

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.040
the next one's slightly further up,

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.320
then slightly further up.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.910
And then it comes back
round and down again

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.090
when you get it back under control

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.026
and you realize what's happening.

00:03:46.026 --> 00:03:49.550
So, obviously you've got
like a huge keyhole there.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:50.781
It's ridiculous isn't it really

00:03:50.781 --> 00:03:53.640
that you're just hurling chunks of metal

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.027
and you're not even really
aiming where you want to be.

00:03:55.027 --> 00:03:58.820
It's just like your body's not
good enough to fire this gun.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.440
I can't not blink.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.188
The first round is
always the most difficult

00:04:03.188 --> 00:04:04.980
and that after that you
sort of get used to it.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.530
All right well thank you
for watching our gun video.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.960
Also thanks to Destin
from Smarter Everyday

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.150
for setting that shoot up.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.240
That was while we were hanging out

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.960
with Destin in Alabama last year.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.380
Had a lot of fun doing
it as well, so yeah.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.560
Yeah, if you like gun stuff

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.200
be sure to check out his channel.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.220
Also, check out the video we
did with underwater pistols.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.810
Follow us both on Twitter.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.960
My Twitter name is GAVINFREE.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.340
Also happens to be my real name.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.360
What about you, Daniel?

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.130
Mine is DANIELGRUCHY.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.667
Again happens to be my real name.

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:31.500
Not gruchy.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.333
Not gruchy.

00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:33.440
Not grouchy.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.170
No, none of those.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.843
Gruchy, technically.

